  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Border Management in the Pacific</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the programme is to contribute to safe and secure Pacific borders being established and promoted through border management and strengthened data collection and sharing systems. The safe re-opening of borders to enable the movement of people and goods through international borders is central to economic recovery from COVID-19 in the Pacific. The Pacific relies heavily on remittances and tourism, both of which have been hindered due to travel restrictions resulting in substantial negative socio-economic impacts on the region&apos;s gross domestic product (GDP). In Fiji and Vanuatu the project will support implementation of MIDAS, the IOM-developed Border Management Information System, a comprehensive system that can support numerous border and migration management functions, enabling governments to easily monitor travelers entering and exiting the national territory, while providing a sound statistical basis for migration and mobility data. In Palau, IOM will support an enabling environment for enhancing integrated border management in Palau based on assessments and reflective of international best practices.</narrative>
  </description>
